  "notes": [
    "The registered adapter creates an ordinary HWND swap chain and back buffer, and its kernel CPU worker completes the first clear. Both attempts reach PresentCb and receive DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED, a positive status that is explicitly not treated as delivered output. No screen-pixel oracle succeeds.",
    "Kernel tracing observes the standard staging allocation size query for 320x192 with pitch initially zero. This KMD supports only GDI standard allocations, so it returns STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED. Windows requires this lockable BGRX8 staging surface for this presentation path. The broader Windows control flow and any additional occlusion conditions were not traced.",
    "Revision a95a58c adds allocation-only metadata for standard BGRX8 staging surfaces, permits BGRA-to-BGRX copies without channel conversion and rejects the reverse alpha-undefined path. Host tests cover allocation lifetime and actual queued rectangle copying; the next signed package must establish live acceptance.",
    "The two successful fences are CPU clears, not NPU execution or presentation. Component NPU execution, registered presentation, DWM migration and Tahoma benefit remain separate acceptance gates."
